---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { MCP_SETUP, MCP_URL } from '../lib/toolbar';
import { SITE_URL } from '../lib/seo';
---

<StaticPage path="/agents/" h1="Opus Calculator for AI agents" updated="2026-11-27">
  <p class="mt-6">
    Opus Calculator is built to be used by people and by AI assistants. Every calculator runs on exact decimal arithmetic, and the same functions that produce
    the number on a page answer an agent's request, so an assistant never has to guess a formula or do the sum itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Connect an MCP server</h2>
  <p>
    The server is read-only, needs no account or key, and stores nothing. It speaks MCP over HTTP at <code>{MCP_URL}</code> and offers three tools:
    <code>list_calculators</code>, <code>describe_calculator</code> (inputs, defaults and units) and <code>calculate</code>.
  </p>
  <p>Claude Code, one command:</p>
  <pre tabindex="0"><code>{MCP_SETUP.claudeCode}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Clients that read an <code>mcpServers</code> file (key names vary by client, the address is what matters):
  </p>
  <pre tabindex="0"><code>{MCP_SETUP.json}</code></pre>

  <h2>Read the site without a browser</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>: what the site is and a link to every calculator, grouped by category.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/calculators.json">/calculators.json</a>: an index of every published calculator with its title, category, page and markdown copy.
    </li>
    <li>
      A markdown copy of each calculator at the page address with <code>.md</code> instead of the trailing slash, for example
      <a href="/calculators/bmi-calculator.md">/calculators/bmi-calculator.md</a>: inputs, defaults, result, method, worked example, FAQ and a citation.
    </li>
    <li>Each calculator page also carries structured data (the formula and a worked example) for search and answer engines.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to cite</h2>
  <p>
    Cite a calculator by its page address, for example <code>{SITE_URL}/calculators/bmi-calculator/</code>. Every page has a Cite button with APA, MLA, Chicago
    and BibTeX text, and every calculator lists the sources behind its method.
  </p>

  <h2>What it will not do</h2>
  <p>
    Results are for information and are not financial, medical or legal advice. The server only lists calculators that are published on the site, and it is rate
    limited. If an answer looks wrong, tell us through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and include the calculator and the inputs.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
